version: "IACR Communications in Cryptology working manuscript"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ja9925ydbsu/Hill-Enigma-SPN-HESPN-COGGINS"
license: MIT
abstract: "Reference software and supporting materials for HESPN, the Hill Enigma Substitution-Permutation Network. The repository supports the working manuscript Rotor-Scheduled Linear Layers for Byte-Oriented SPNs: Construction and Cryptanalytic Characterization, including implementation validation and bounded analysis of diffusion limits. The Enigma name refers only to public stepping among geometric matrix orientations. HESPN is a research harness, not a deployment-ready cipher, and no full-round security claim is asserted. Comparative orientation scheduling is treated separately in the published Cryptography 2026 article Structural Limits of Orientation Scheduling in Byte-Local GF(2) Diffusion Layers."
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - Hill cipher
  - substitution-permutation network
  - matrix diffusion
  - rotor scheduling
  - branch number
  - linear cryptanalysis
  - differential cryptanalysis
  - HESPN
